<ArticleLayout title={page.title} hreflang={hreflang} description={page.description} canonical={page.canonical} author={page.author} date={page.date} ogImage="/images/Does-Milk-Thistle-Expire-3.jpg" bodyHtml={`<p><a href="/milk-thistle-seed-bulk-north-china-production/">Milk thistle</a>, known scientifically as <em>Silybum marianum</em>, is a time-tested herbal remedy praised for its liver-protective effects. But like any natural product, it doesn’t last forever. <strong>Does milk thistle expire?</strong> <strong>Do milk thistle supplements go bad?</strong> These are questions we get often from bulk buyers and health-conscious consumers.</p><p>In this comprehensive guide, we’ll explore:</p><ol><li>What is milk thistle?</li><li>What part of milk thistle is used?</li><li>Nutritional analysis and comparison of active components</li><li>What happens when milk thistle goes bad</li><li>Proper storage &amp; ideal product forms for long-term use</li><li>Some FAQs like: <em>Do milk thistle supplements go bad? How long does milk thistle last?</em></li><li>Data-backed conclusions for bulk buyers</li></ol><hr/><h2></h2><h2>1. What Is Milk Thistle?</h2><p>Milk thistle is a flowering plant native to the Mediterranean region and commonly used as an herbal supplement. Its seeds contain <strong>silymarin</strong>, a group of flavonolignans with antioxidant, anti-inflammatory, and hepatoprotective properties.</p><p>Milk thistle has been used in traditional medicine for over 2,000 years, mainly for liver and gallbladder disorders.</p><hr/><h2><img alt="Does Milk Thistle Expire" height="565" src="/images/Does-Milk-Thistle-Expire-300x300.jpg" width="565"/></h2><h2>2. What Part of Milk Thistle Is Used?</h2><p>The <strong>seeds (also called achenes)</strong> of milk thistle are the primary part used for medicinal purposes. Sometimes, the whole fruit or crushed seed powder is used in teas and capsules.</p><h3>Common forms:</h3><ul><li>Whole milk thistle seeds (raw)</li><li>Ground seed powder</li><li>Silymarin extract (standardized 70–80%)</li><li>Oil (cold-pressed from seeds)</li></ul><hr/><h2>3. Nutritional Analysis of Milk Thistle Parts</h2><table border="1" cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Whole Seed (per 100g)</th><th>Ground Powder</th><th>Silymarin Extract (80%)</th><th>Cold-Pressed Oil</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Silymarin</strong></td><td>4–6%</td><td>4–6%</td><td>70–80%</td><td>Trace</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Fat (mostly PUFA)</strong></td><td>25–30g</td><td>25–30g</td><td>&lt;1g</td><td>~98g</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Protein</strong></td><td>18–20g</td><td>18–20g</td><td>&lt;1g</td><td>0g</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shelf Life Estimate</strong></td><td>1–2 years</td><td>12–18 months</td><td>2–3 years</td><td>6–12 months</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"></div></div><p><strong>Source:</strong></p><ul><li>European Medicines Agency (EMA, 2018)</li><li>U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) Database</li><li>National Institutes of Health (NIH) Herbal Supplement Facts</li></ul><hr/><h2>4. What Happens When Milk Thistle Goes Bad?</h2><p>When expired or improperly stored, milk thistle may lose potency or develop harmful by-products:</p><ul><li><strong>Silymarin degradation</strong>: Reduced antioxidant activity (source: Journal of Pharmacy and Pharmacology, 2014)</li><li><strong>Rancid oils</strong>: Cold-pressed oil oxidizes, forming <strong>aldehydes and ketones</strong>, which are cytotoxic.</li><li><strong>Mycotoxin risk</strong>: Moisture exposure may lead to mold growth, especially <strong>Aspergillus flavus</strong>, which can produce <strong>aflatoxins</strong>, known liver carcinogens.</li></ul><blockquote><p>💡 According to a 2021 study in <em>Food Control</em>, improperly stored milk thistle seeds showed a 3.4% contamination rate with detectable aflatoxins in humid conditions above 65% RH.</p></blockquote><hr/><h2><img alt="Does Milk Thistle Expire" height="575" src="/images/Does-Milk-Thistle-Expire-2-300x300.jpg" width="575"/></h2><h2>5. Best Storage Practices &amp; Ideal Product Forms</h2><h3> Storage Tips:</h3><ul><li>Store in <strong>airtight containers</strong></li><li>Keep in a <strong>cool, dry place (&lt;25°C / 77°F)</strong></li><li>Avoid <strong>sunlight &amp; humidity</strong></li></ul><h3>Product Types Better for Long-Term Storage:</h3><table border="1" cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead><tr><th>Product Type</th><th>Shelf Life</th><th>Best Packaging</th><th>Cost Efficiency for Bulk</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Whole Seed</td><td>18–24 mo</td><td>Vacuum-sealed PE bags</td><td>★★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>Silymarin Extract</td><td>24–36 mo</td><td>Aluminum foil pouches</td><td>★★★★☆</td></tr><tr><td>Ground Powder</td><td>12–18 mo</td><td>Airtight HDPE containers</td><td>★★★☆☆</td></tr><tr><td>Cold-Pressed Oil</td><td>6–12 mo</td><td>Amber glass bottles</td><td>★★☆☆☆</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"></div></div><h3>Bulk Purchasing Tip:</h3><blockquote><p>Choose <strong>whole seeds</strong> or <strong>standardized silymarin extracts</strong> with <strong>COA</strong> and <strong>moisture &lt;8%</strong>, vacuum-sealed in aluminum or PE inner bags with outer cartons.</p></blockquote><hr/><h2>6. FAQs:</h2><h3><strong>Does milk thistle expire?</strong></h3><p>Yes, milk thistle expires like all natural products. Depending on form and storage, its shelf life ranges from <strong>6 months to 3 years</strong>.</p><h3><strong>Do milk thistle supplements go bad?</strong></h3><p>Yes. Expired milk thistle supplements may lose potency and could become rancid or contaminated with mold. Always check <strong>expiry dates</strong> and <strong>packaging integrity</strong>.</p><h3><strong>How long does milk thistle last?</strong></h3><ul><li>Whole seed: up to 24 months</li><li>Extract: up to 36 months</li><li>Powder: 12–18 months</li><li>Oil: 6–12 months</li></ul><hr/><h2>7. Conclusion: What Buyers Need to Know</h2><p>Based on verified data and research from the EMA, USDA, and peer-reviewed journals, <strong>milk thistle’s shelf life depends heavily on its form and storage conditions</strong>. Bulk buyers looking for maximum shelf life and quality assurance should prioritize <strong>standardized extracts or vacuum-packed whole seeds</strong>.</p><p>If you’re sourcing <strong>milk thistle seeds, powder, or extracts in bulk</strong>, visit our <a href="#" rel="noopener"><strong>Product Page</strong></a> to explore:</p><ul><li>Full COA + 3rd party testing</li><li>Packaging customized for export</li><li>Competitive wholesale pricing</li><li>Global delivery from certified production bases</li></ul><hr/><h3><a href="/milk-thistle-seed-bulk-north-china-production/">Explore Bulk Milk Thistle Products →</a></h3><hr/><h2>References</h2><ol><li>EMA. (2018). <em>Assessment report on Silybum marianum (L.) Gaertn., fructus</em>. European Medicines Agency.</li><li>NIH Office of Dietary Supplements. (2022). <em>Milk Thistle Fact Sheet</em>.</li><li>Journal of Pharmacy and Pharmacology (2014). “Silymarin Stability in Herbal Formulations”.</li><li>USDA FoodData Central.</li><li><em>Food Control</em>, Volume 123, 2021: “Aflatoxin contamination risk in stored milk thistle seeds.”</li></ol>`} />
